  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;SANDUSKY TOWNSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sandusky Township is one of the sixteen townships of Crawford County, Ohio, United States, known for its population and governance structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRAWFORD COUNTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crawford County is a county in Ohio, containing Sandusky Township and other townships, with a population of 1,234 as of the 2020 census."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OHIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ohio is a state in the United States, containing Crawford County and Sandusky Township."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SANDUSKY RIVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Sandusky River flows through the southern part of Sandusky Township, giving it its name."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RICHLAND COUNTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Richland County contains other Sandusky Townships, distinct from Sandusky Township in Crawford County."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SANDUSKY COUNTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sandusky County contains other Sandusky Townships, distinct from Sandusky Township in Crawford County."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNITED STATES CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The United States Census provides population data for Sandusky Township, including counts from 2010 and 2020."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDITOR UNITED STATES CENSUS BUREAU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Editor United States Census Bureau is responsible for compiling and publishing census data."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAR OWNERSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Car Ownership refers to the distribution of households in Sandusky County based on the number of cars owned."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPER COMMUTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Super Commutes refer to travel times exceeding 90 minutes within Sandusky County, OH."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Males are mentioned in relation to median income statistics in Sandusky County, OH."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEMALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Females are mentioned in relation to median income statistics in Sandusky County, OH."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COUNTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"County is used generically to refer to Sandusky County, OH, in discussions of demographics and politics."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEMOGRAPHICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Demographics include population statistics, income levels, and poverty rates in Sandusky County, OH."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLITICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Politics includes historical voting patterns and current political leanings of Crawford County, OH."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NO MUNICIPALITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"No municipalities are located in Sandusky Township, indicating its rural nature without urban centers."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THREE-MEMBER BOARD OF TRUSTEES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The township is governed by a three-member board of trustees, who are elected to represent the community."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOVEMBER OF ODD-NUMBERED YEARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TIME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trustees are elected in November of odd-numbered years, indicating a regular election cycle."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOUR-YEAR TERM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TIME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trustees serve a four-year term beginning on the following January, indicating a defined governance period."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EASTERN PART OF THE COUNTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sandusky Township is located in the eastern part of Crawford County, providing a geographical reference."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOUTHERN PART OF THE TOWNSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Sandusky River flows through the southern part of Sandusky Township, highlighting a geographical feature."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1,234 (2020 CENSUS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POPULATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"As of the 2020 census, the population of Sandusky Township was 1,234, providing recent demographic data."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1,234 (2010 CENSUS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POPULATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"As of the 2010 census, the population of Sandusky Township was 1,234, providing historical demographic data."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;10.8% OF FAMILIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POPULATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"About 10.8% of families in Sandusky County were below the poverty line, indicating socio-economic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;13.0% OF THE POPULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POPULATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"About 13.0% of the population in Sandusky County were below the poverty line, indicating socio-economic conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;21.3% OF THOSE UNDER AGE 18&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POPULATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"21.3% of those under age 18 in Sandusky County were below the poverty line, indicating socio-economic conditions for youth."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;6.2% OF THOSE AGE 65 OR OVER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POPULATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"6.2% of those age 65 or over in Sandusky County were below the poverty line, indicating socio-economic conditions for the elderly."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRONGLY DEMOCRATIC COUNTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POLITICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prior to 1924, Crawford County was a strongly Democratic county, indicating historical political leanings."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRONGLY REPUBLICAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POLITICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Since 1924, Crawford County has become strongly Republican, indicating a shift in political leanings."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0045-9fddedc4e7ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDIAN HOUSEHOLD INCOME&quot;">
